From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: add the SmartSens SC2336 sensor driver

Add a mainline V4L2 subdev driver for the SC2336, a 1920x1080 10-bit
Bayer sensor used on most Ingenic T31 camera models. The mode register
sequence and the 161-step analogue gain table come from the Ingenic
vendor sensor driver.

The sensor uses 16-bit register addresses, so the driver instantiates
the CCI regmap with a 16-bit address width. Exposure is a 20-bit value
in 1/16-line units; HTS/VTS, gain, and mirror/flip are exposed through
standard V4L2 controls.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- /dev/null
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/sc2336.c
@@ -0,0 +1,910 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
+/*
+ * SmartSens SC2336 CMOS Image Sensor Driver
+ *
+ * The register sequences and gain table are adapted from the Ingenic
+ * vendor sensor driver (sensor_sc2336_t31).
+ */
+
+#include <linux/clk.h>
+#include <linux/delay.h>
+#include <linux/gpio/consumer.h>
+#include <linux/i2c.h>
